{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 49, :comments ["<b>Until they ceased, etc.</b> Meaning: they ceased counting the storehouses of grain belonging to Yosef, because there is no number of those bringing it — they would not count on account of the trouble involved in counting, and they did not measure what they would bring. And although they would bring a fifth, as we explained in the verse ״וְחִמֵּשׁ״, even so they would divide the grain into five parts and set aside one part, and they did not know how much it amounted to in the total brought. And this is the measure of the verse: ״עַד כִּי חָדַל סוֹפְרוֹ שֶׁל יוֹסֵף לִסְפֹּר כִּי אֵין מִסְפָּר״ — for the grain from those bringing it, and one would need to count each item and tally the sum; therefore he ceased counting."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:47:47.093762680Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}